{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion","id":1357148,"title":"What are the most interesting parts of Aeon Aexpansion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-26T19:10:05-08:00","id":1357148,"title":"What are the most interesting parts of Aeon Aexpansion?","content":"I was thinking about buying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T19:23:38-08:00","id":1357149,"title":"","content":"Pretty much? Everything. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, I'd say that psiads are probably the most interesting, especially if you want to run settings with psionics in other eras. Superiors are also good, whether you intend them to be set in this timeline or if you're looking for superhumans that aren't as obvious as psis and novas to put in a different age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T19:53:54-08:00","id":1357153,"title":"","content":"That sounds great! Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T00:02:28-08:00","id":1357173,"title":"","content":"For me it's the rules for Superiors and Psiads, though most of the book (ideas for Psions outside of Aeon aside) is highly useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T07:18:47-08:00","id":1357195,"title":"","content":"Personally I most enjoyed the section on technology in the early 22nd century and how it is integrated and used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T10:46:43-08:00","id":1357216,"title":"","content":"The section on Superiors and Psiads are AWESOME and entirely worthy on their own. The section on Psions in other periods, including the modern day, is also fantastic. When I get in a technology mood the section about technology would be very useful as well. <br /> <br /> Sooooo basically, as a summation, the whole book is awesome and sooooo very much worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T11:06:51-08:00","id":1357221,"title":"","content":"Every chapter has at least some gold in it.<br /> <br /> The story hooks from the Aberrant and Aberrant Cults section are almost indispensable. It really expands the possibilities of what combating Aberrants can be other than a bunch of monsters showing up in Sydney.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T12:17:46-08:00","id":1357230,"title":"","content":"This is really helpful. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T13:26:04-08:00","id":1357245,"title":"","content":"Just as a reminder, \u00c6xpansion is an expansion on Aeon and need it to play. If you are planning to buy and don\u2019t have Aeon, buy it first.<br /> <br /> The technology chapters are an addon to the equipments and tags we see in Aeon.<br /> <br /> Psiads use the psion powers.<br /> <br /> The only thing that is straight forward from Core is the Superiors (need Aeon for the backstory, not for the rules).<br /> <br /> Otherwise this book is gold... even better than the hope we had before it comes to backers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T14:20:33-08:00","id":1357253,"title":"","content":"I have it and I loved it. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T18:58:06-08:00","id":1357437,"title":"","content":"I loved Aeon Aexpansion! When we play Aeon I\u2019m gonna play a Superior with Social Forte and maybe some Mental Powers as backup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T15:45:51-08:00","id":1357621,"title":"","content":"I ordered it today in hardcopy. (for a number of reasons, I tend to avoid pdf stuff as much as possible) I figure it'll get here well after \u00c6ON, which I'm ordering off Amazon after New Years. I'm looking forward to Psiads, as I have an idea for a historical setting with them. ATM I'm enjoying the core book quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T16:37:33-08:00","id":1357636,"title":"","content":"Both books are amazing. What\u2019s your historical setting about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T17:43:23-08:00","id":1357648,"title":"","content":"I just ordered it in physical copy as there is no way that I did not want a copy of it to be sitting next to my Aeon stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T18:20:07-08:00","id":1357922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1357636#post1357636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both books are amazing. What\u2019s your historical setting about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been fiddling with the idea of Aquarius, about the great psionic awakening in the late 1960s. It would probably use 1974, the year Stephen King's Carrie was published, as its default date. Besides that novel, it'd likely draw on a number of usual sources involving aliens, LSD culture, witch covens, weird conspiracy theories, and a certain level of Philip K Dick-ness. Probably also an appearance by Gary Gygax as a psychic guru of the Midwest.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also wanting to do my 1970s action-adventure setting with all of the types that were in the original Adventure!, but I haven't thought of a good name for it yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T14:13:17-08:00","id":1358079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1357922#post1357922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been fiddling with the idea of Aquarius, about the great psionic awakening in the late 1960s. It would probably use 1974, the year Stephen King's Carrie was published, as its default date. Besides that novel, it'd likely draw on a number of usual sources involving aliens, LSD culture, witch covens, weird conspiracy theories, and a certain level of Philip K Dick-ness. Probably also an appearance by Gary Gygax as a psychic guru of the Midwest.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also wanting to do my 1970s action-adventure setting with all of the types that were in the original Adventure!, but I haven't thought of a good name for it yet.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Age of Groove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T14:23:02-08:00","id":1358083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> fascinating! Thank you \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T16:54:04-08:00","id":1358105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358079#post1358079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Age of Groove.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Action! maybe, but that may be more suitable to an 80s thing. For the 70s thing, I'm aiming for something that encompasses The Shaft novels and films (including his Superior/Stalwart counterpart Luke Cage), The Destroyer novels, the Mack Bolan/Executioner novels (which were clearly an influence on Marvel's Punisher), Bruce Lee and his films, The Six-Million Dollar Man and The Bionic Woman (and the Martin Caidin novels that inspired them), Eval Knievel, The Man from Atlantis, The Invisible Man/Gemini Man, SHAZAM! and The Secrets of Iris, Charlie's Angels and Toni's Boys, Starsky &amp; Hutch, McMillan &amp; Wife, McCloud, Smokey and the Bandit, period Westerns, the Roger Moore era James Bond films, Saga of the Swamp Thing and Man Thing, Iron Fist, The Daughters of the Dragon, Master of Kung Fu, Sons of the Tiger and White Tiger, Bronze Tiger, Warlord, Devil Dinosaur, and a lot of the decade's Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T12:53:09-08:00","id":1358230,"title":"","content":"In terms of using Psions, my big idea is an Edwardian setting where the War of the Worlds happened as Wells lay out in the 1890s, and the left over alien tech has allowed humanity to create Psi Orders by 1910.<br /> <br /> Whether this will result in an even more catastrophic Great War is up to the player characters\u2019 actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T12:56:39-08:00","id":1358232,"title":"","content":"I also want to do a Planetary Romance set in a timeline where Adventure! protagonists stopped the rise of fascism and WW2, but that will have Mesmerists and Stalwarts in an alternate mid-20th Century rather than Psions. May use Psionic modes for some of the aliens though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T13:29:43-08:00","id":1358235,"title":"","content":"I would love to have an Edwardian/Victorian setting with Psiads doing all the moving chairs, seances and all the supernatural phenomena that popped up in that period. A cross of Sherlock Holmes and Frankistein would be the easy result, but what I had in mind was more supernatural, witches, vampires and spirits being studied by some adventurous parapsychologists and mediums.<br /> <br /> I will create a new post for discussing this idea...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T13:41:22-08:00","id":1358237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358235#post1358235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to have an Edwardian/Victorian setting with Psiads doing all the moving chairs, seances and all the supernatural phenomena that popped up in that period. A cross of Sherlock Holmes and Frankistein would be the easy result, but what I had in mind was more supernatural, witches, vampires and spirits being studied by some adventurous parapsychologists and mediums.<br /> <br /> I will create a new post for discussing this idea...</div> </div> </div> </div>just to note, I think if you want something evoking the powers ascribed to Mediums and the like in the era, Mesmerists are probably going to be more appropriate than Psiads and Psions. The point of my Edwardian setting is the world is being flung into full scifi way early, rather than accurately evoking the fiction and superstitions of the era around psychic abilities.<br /> <br /> I have an idea for a Victorian setting with the monsters you\u2019re getting at, but I\u2019ll save that for your other thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T13:46:02-08:00","id":1358239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358232#post1358232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want to do a Planetary Romance set in a timeline where Adventure! protagonists stopped the rise of fascism and WW2, but that will have Mesmerists and Stalwarts in an alternate mid-20th Century rather than Psions. May use Psionic modes for some of the aliens though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. An early 21st century where Italian Fascism, Soviet Communism, and Japanese militarism all collapse in the 1920s, and the Weimar Republic and Republic of China survive (and eventually thrive), and Goddard's rocket work had men reaching the moon by his death in 1945 and Martian colonies in the 60s. (Also Jacques Cousteau helping create France's first undersea colonies in the 60s.) Then maybe alien contact in the 60s or 70s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T13:52:07-08:00","id":1358240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358239#post1358239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. An early 21st century where Italian Fascism, Soviet Communism, and Japanese militarism all collapse in the 1920s, and the Weimar Republic and Republic of China survive (and eventually thrive), and Goddard's rocket work had men reaching the moon by his death in 1945 and Martian colonies in the 60s. (Also Jacques Cousteau helping create France's first undersea colonies in the 60s.) Then maybe alien contact in the 60s or 70s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking going fuller alternate cosmology to be true to the genre, with Martian princesses and Venusian jungles.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like the various pulp locations in Adventure! They exist in parallel timelines and end up overlapping. In this timeline the Inspiration Age never ends so they never go out of sync.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:58:18-08:00","id":1358291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358230#post1358230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of using Psions, my big idea is an Edwardian setting where the War of the Worlds happened as Wells lay out in the 1890s, and the left over alien tech has allowed humanity to create Psi Orders by 1910.<br /> <br /> Whether this will result in an even more catastrophic Great War is up to the player characters\u2019 actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may find it worthwhile to track down a copy of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_Traces\" target=\"_blank\">Scarlet Traces</a>. &quot;<i>Scarlet Traces</i> is based on the premise that Britain was able to reverse engineer alien technology, abandoned after the abortive Martian invasion of The War of the Worlds, to establish economic and political dominance over the remainder of the world. The artwork shows an imposition of futuristic devices on early 20th-century society. In the first series, set in 1908, London cabbies and the Household Cavalry have swapped their horses for mechanical devices with spiderlike legs; homes are heated and lit by modified versions of the Martian heat ray; the pigeons of Trafalgar Square are thinned out by miniature Martian war machines.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T22:45:14-08:00","id":1358354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358240#post1358240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking going fuller alternate cosmology to be true to the genre, with Martian princesses and Venusian jungles.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like the various pulp locations in Adventure! They exist in parallel timelines and end up overlapping. In this timeline the Inspiration Age never ends so they never go out of sync.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. In that case the 45 moon missions might come across moon people from 19th and early 20th century fiction, and later a Mars that is a mix of John Carter and The Martian Chronicles with a little of Stranger in a Strange Land mixed in. Then the various alien races living in the moons of Jupiter and Saturn. Meanwhile, various nations have been making expeditions to the Hollow Earth and the lands beneath the Antarctic ice since the 30s. <br /> <br /> Somewhere I have the Space 1889 guide to the planets which included an interesting take on Mercury that would also work well with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T03:34:21-08:00","id":1358388,"title":"","content":"Just for general information, I just bought my POD of Core, In Media Res, \u00c6on and \u00c6xpansion.<br /> <br /> it will arrive in 2-6 weeks + 2-5 weekdays... basically sometime in February...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T08:44:19-08:00","id":1358424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358354#post1358354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. In that case the 45 moon missions might come across moon people from 19th and early 20th century fiction, and later a Mars that is a mix of John Carter and The Martian Chronicles with a little of Stranger in a Strange Land mixed in. Then the various alien races living in the moons of Jupiter and Saturn. Meanwhile, various nations have been making expeditions to the Hollow Earth and the lands beneath the Antarctic ice since the 30s.<br /> <br /> Somewhere I have the Space 1889 guide to the planets which included an interesting take on Mercury that would also work well with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Toss in some Mi-go living on Pluto and being angry about it no longer being considered a planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T22:53:42-08:00","id":1358553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358424#post1358424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Toss in some Mi-go living on Pluto and being angry about it no longer being considered a planet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IT is a planet. That humans deny Yugoth as a planet is just their small minds missing the greater universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T04:18:29-08:00","id":1358585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1358553#post1358553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> IT is a planet. That humans deny Yugoth as a planet is just their small minds missing the greater universe.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S4E2ZuPCBG0&amp;feature=emb_title\" target=\"_blank\">So, the Mi-go are a bunch of Space Jerrys.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T19:51:11-08:00","id":1358755,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that this space opera/planetary romance thing needs Tesla's energy broadcasting system (as well as teleforce guns and violet ray medical tech). Probably a lot of Buckminster Fuller designed geodesic dome architecture mixed with art deco as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-03-2020, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T20:09:17-08:00","id":1358987,"title":"","content":"You know, the funny thing? The Mi Go are probably the most reasonable of the Lovecratian critters, save for the Elder Things. They were prefectly happy to keep mining their ores, trading trinkets with the locals who helped them, and when the guy started probing and investigating, they spent something like six months gradually escalating their campaign of &quot;Stop poking&quot; even as he killed a few of them (remembering that they could have zorched him from the beginning), before they finally said: hell with it, brain jar it is. <br /> <br /> So when you get right down to it, they were far more restrained than most humans would have been.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T04:49:47-08:00","id":1359048,"title":"","content":"DriveThruRPG says my copy of \u00c6xpansion has shipped, yay!<br /> <br /> My copy of \u00c6on came the other day and I'm still digesting it. It and the core book are both impressive and very smart looking books. Kudos to everyone who worked on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T05:20:50-08:00","id":1359049,"title":"","content":"Thank you! I hope you enjoy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T13:51:49-08:00","id":1359130,"title":"","content":"My physical copy has arrived to much rejoicing and flipping and bookmarking - the old fashioned way, with bits of paper. hehe<br /> <br /> I really, REALLY, like the AEon Expansion book and so to have it with the other two books is brilliant to me. <br /> <br /> It also gave me another idea about a setting with Superiors as the default group, maybe even them in a sort of medieval fantasy setting. Or maybe one that looks medieval fantasy but is actually scifi - all thanks to the founding Novas that set the colony up before going elsewhere upon reaching Quantum 10 - with rulership being given to the powered class pf Superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T20:44:20-08:00","id":1359203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1357148-what-are-the-most-interesting-parts-of-aeon-aexpansion?p=1359130#post1359130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also gave me another idea about a setting with Superiors as the default group, maybe even them in a sort of medieval fantasy setting. Or maybe one that looks medieval fantasy but is actually scifi - all thanks to the founding Novas that set the colony up before going elsewhere upon reaching Quantum 10 - with rulership being given to the powered class pf Superiors.</div> </div> </div> </div>You find bits of that in Arthurian lore. Sir Galahad having the strength of ten men and Sir Ironside's great strength and resistance to damage.<br /> <br /> A viking style setting with&quot;troll-blooded&quot; characters with inhuman strength and other abilities would also be pretty cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}